menu "ESP Real-Time Diagnostics"

    config ESP_RT_DIAGNOSTICS_ENABLE
        bool "Enable real-time diagnostic snapshots"
        default y
        help
            Collect bounded timing statistics and event counters inside
            deterministic tasks. This enables cycle, ISR-to-task wake,
            deadline, missed-event, and application-event accounting.

            Disable this option after development to compile the inline
            instrumentation into no-ops in the critical path. The out-of-line
            snapshot and derived-value symbols remain linkable, but an
            application normally compile-gates its accumulator and reporter.

    config ESP_RT_DIAGNOSTICS_DETAILED_TIMING
        bool "Measure named stages and periodic intervals"
        depends on ESP_RT_DIAGNOSTICS_ENABLE
        default y
        help
            Collect per-stage average/maximum execution times, configured
            budget violations, and min/max intervals. Core cycle,
            missed-event, error, and deadline counters remain part of the base
            diagnostics when this option is disabled.

            Each stage_begin/stage_end pair reads esp_timer, so leave this off
            when only aggregate deadline evidence is required or when
            characterizing the instrumentation's own cost.

    config ESP_RT_DIAGNOSTICS_WINDOW_MS
        int "Diagnostic snapshot window (ms)"
        depends on ESP_RT_DIAGNOSTICS_ENABLE
        range 100 3600000
        default 5000
        help
            Default duration accumulated before a diagnostic snapshot becomes
            due. Each esp_rt_diag_config_t may override it with its own
            window_duration_us, allowing independent monitoring windows for
            tasks with different periods.

endmenu
